    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭtyca</span></b> , ae, or
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭtycē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοτύκα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Sicily, between Camarina and
			Syracuse</i>, now <i>Modica</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 14,
				268</span></i>.— Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭtycensis</span></b> , e, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Mutyce</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 3, 43, § 101</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 3, 51, § 120</span></i>.—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mŭty-censes</span></b> ,
			ĭum, m., <i>the
				inhabitants of Mutyca</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 8,
				14, § 91</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
